// COMPAT-513 (archived to examples/compat/ by №533): historical syntax — not parsed since v0.27.x. See rule №513 (gh#797).
// COMPAT-513: the file is a CONTRACT for a future implementation (deferred respond) — it declares itself 'intentionally NOT in the test suite'; checking it now would invent behavior. Do NOT invent a check — the rewrite is a separate naryad.
// №581 (gh#995): the RESPOND_NOT_TERMINAL gate flags the bare mid-route respond recorded below (the repo sweep found exactly this one hit, 355 .mlog files scanned). The file is NOT migrated: the deferred semantics ("code after respond() continues") is the OPPOSITE of the return-form — the future deferred-response naryad must express the contract in sanctioned shapes.
// ── Наряд #69 Block 2: Deferred route response contract ──────────────────
//
// This contract is for FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION (separate narad).
// It defines the acceptance criteria for deferred route response:
// code after respond() continues executing in the background.
//
// Expected behavior (when implemented):
//   1. Client receives "200 ok" within 100ms
//   2. File "deferred_marker.txt" appears AFTER the response was sent,
//      confirming that code after respond() actually executed.
//
// This file is intentionally NOT in the test suite — it serves as
// a contract for the implementation narad.

mlogserver {
  port: 10199
  host: "127.0.0.1"

  route "/webhook" method=POST {
    let data = parse_json(request_body())
    respond("200 ok")
    write_file("deferred_marker.txt", "done")
  }
}
